- How would you adapt this to be stable?
- How does memory usage change with large datasets?

## Why This Is Asked
Assesses augmenting a Trie to answer prefix-based queries with dynamic weights while maintaining efficient updates. Encourages careful handling of edge cases and update semantics.

## Key Concepts
- Trie augmentation with maxSubtreeWeight; non-decreasing weight updates.
- O(len(word)) insert and O(len(s)) query.
- Edge cases: empty word input, overlapping prefixes, no matches.

## Code Example
```javascript
class Node {
  constructor() {
    this.next = new Map();
    this.wordWeight = 0;
    this.hasWord = false;
    this.maxSubtreeWeight = 0;
  }
}
class PrefixWeightTrie {
  constructor() { this.root = new Node(); }
  insert(word, weight) {
    let node = this.root;
    for (const ch of word) {
      if (!node.next.has(ch)) node.next.set(ch, new Node());
      node = node.next.get(ch);
    }
    if (!node.hasWord || weight > node.wordWeight) {
      node.hasWord = true;
      node.wordWeight = weight;
    }
    // update maxSubtreeWeight along path (omitted detailed propagation for brevity)
  }
  queryLongestPrefix(s) {
    let node = this.root;
    let bestLen = 0, bestWeight = 0;
    for (let i = 0; i < s.length; i++) {
      const c = s[i];
      if (!node.next.has(c)) break;
      node = node.next.get(c);
      if (node.maxSubtreeWeight > 0) {
        bestLen = i + 1;
        bestWeight = node.maxSubtreeWeight;
      }
    }
    return [bestLen, bestWeight];
  }
}
```

## Why This Question Is Asked
This question tests dynamic programming intuition on a constrained path counting problem with simple transitions and boundary conditions.

## Key Concepts
- **Recurrence relation:** f(i) = f(i+1) + f(i+2) with modulo arithmetic
- **Memoization vs. tabulation:** Trade-offs between recursive top-down with caching versus iterative bottom-up approaches
- **Edge conditions:** Blocked start/end positions, single-cell arrays

## Code Example
```javascript
function countPaths(blocked) {
  const n = blocked.length;
  const MOD = 1000000007;
  if (blocked[0]) return 0;

  // Memoized DFS
  const memo = Array(n).fill(-1);
  function dfs(i) {
    if (i === n - 1) return blocked[i] ? 0 : 1;
    if (i >= n || blocked[i]) return 0;
    if (memo[i] !== -1) return memo[i];
    memo[i] = (dfs(i + 1) + dfs(i + 2)) % MOD;
    return memo[i];
  }
  return dfs(0);
}

// Bottom-up DP (O(1) space)
function countPathsDP(blocked) {
  const n = blocked.length;
  const MOD = 1000000007;
  if (blocked[0]) return 0;

  let next2 = 1, next1 = blocked[n - 1] ? 0 : 1;
  for (let i = n - 2; i >= 0; i--) {
    const curr = blocked[i] ? 0 : (next1 + next2) % MOD;
    next2 = next1;
    next1 = curr;
  }
  return next1;
}
```

